window.docContents[144].resolve({"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Fs.Ioctl/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Fs___Ioctl":{"contents":"Paper › arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Fs › Ioctl.leanTier 3 · arm64-semantics\n\nTier 3 · arm64-semantics used by the symbolic proof 2 headline theorems depend on it 56 of 86 lines trusted source ↗Trusted, reviewed with the engine. The AArch64 model in arm64-semantics is Tier 3: it is reviewed in its own repository (check-trust-guards). The declarations that the headline statements use are shown for completeness.\n\nDeclarations on this page (9)def SYS_IOCTLdef FIONREAD_W32def FIONBIO_W32def FIONCLEX_W32def FIOCLEX_W32def FIOASYNC_W32def FIOQSIZE_W32def isTtyOnlyIoctldef execIoctl\n\nLinux VFS ioctl SyscallModels Linux AArch64 ioctl (__NR_ioctl = 29, fs/ioctl.c SYSCALL_DEFINE3(ioctl) and do_vfs_ioctl), covering FIOCLEX, FIONCLEX, FIONREAD on regular files, and -ENOTTY for terminal-only 'T' commands on regular files.\n\n\n\ndef SYS_IOCTLL26–27 ↗#Linux AArch64 ioctl syscall number (__NR_ioctl = 29, include/uapi/asm-generic/unistd.h:111, fs/ioctl.c:583).\n\ndef FIONREAD_W32L29–32 ↗#Generic VFS ioctl commands (include/uapi/asm-generic/ioctls.h:46,53,85-87,106): FIONREAD (0x541B), FIONBIO (0x5421), FIONCLEX (0x5450), FIOCLEX (0x5451), FIOASYNC (0x5452), and FIOQSIZE (0x5460), all handled by do_vfs_ioctl before vfs_ioctl.\n\ndef FIONBIO_W32L33 ↗#\n\ndef FIONCLEX_W32L34 ↗#\n\ndef FIOCLEX_W32L35 ↗#\n\ndef FIOASYNC_W32L36 ↗#\n\ndef FIOQSIZE_W32L37 ↗#\n\ndef isTtyOnlyIoctlL39–45 ↗#cmd is a terminal (_IOC_TYPE(cmd) == 'T', include/uapi/asm-generic/ioctls.h) command that do_vfs_ioctl (fs/ioctl.c:492) does not handle itself, so on a regular file it falls through file_ioctl -> vfs_ioctl and returns -ENOTTY.\n\ndef execIoctlL47–84 ↗#ioctl(fd, cmd, arg) (__NR_ioctl = 29, fs/ioctl.c:583 SYSCALL_DEFINE3(ioctl) -> do_vfs_ioctl at fs/ioctl.c:492), reading the low 32 bits of X1 as unsigned int cmd:* closed fds ≥ 3 and negative fds return -EBADF;* FIOCLEX / FIONCLEX on open .localFile or .localDir descriptors set / clear FdEntry.cloexec and return 0 (set_close_on_exec);* FIONREAD on .localFile stores the 32-bit int i_size - f_pos (truncated, as by put_user(i_size_read(inode) - filp->f_pos, (int __user *)argp)) at arg and returns 0, or returns -EFAULT if arg is not 4-byte writable;* terminal-only cmds (isTtyOnlyIoctl, e.g. TCGETS, TIOCGWINSZ) on .localFile return -ENOTTY, assuming the file system's unlocked_ioctl handles no 'T' commands;* [INTENTIONAL_SCOPE]: other cmds on .localFile (FIONBIO, FIOASYNC, FIOQSIZE, FIGETBSZ, FS_IOC_*, ...), unmodeled stdio fds, other cmds on .localDir, and other descriptor kinds trap fail-closed.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"arm64-semantics/Arm64/Trusted/Syscalls/Fs/Ioctl.lean","id":"/Tier-3___-trusted___-not-read/AArch64-semantics/Arm64.Trusted.Syscalls.Fs.Ioctl/#file-Arm64___Trusted___Syscalls___Fs___Ioctl"}});